// Demonstrates BlazeLang's eval(): parses and evaluates a string as a
// single BlazeLang expression, using the same Lexer -> Parser ->
// Interpreter pipeline as the rest of the language (no Python eval()/
// exec() involved), with full access to the current scope.

var x = 10
var y = 20

Show(eval("x + y"))

Function Add(a, b) {
    return a + b
}

Show(eval("Add(5, 10)"))
